{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>The beginning.</b> Because he mentioned that He is awesome, he said: \"The beginning of wisdom is fear of YHWH.\" \"Good understanding belongs to all who do His precepts,\" and each of those who do His praise stands forever, like the daughters of Tzelafchad. And it is possible that the vav of \"His praise\" returns to \"good understanding.\" And Rabbi Moses said: for the heh and mem of עושיהם (their doers) return to wisdom and fear, and the meaning is that those who act according to their obligation and in the manner they should acknowledge."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 111, :notes {0 "The phrase 'בנות צעדה עלי שור' appears garbled; it may be a corruption of 'בנות צלפחד' (the daughters of Tzelafchad), whose praise endured. Translated hyper-literally as 'the daughters of Tzeda upon ox.' The epithet 'Rabbi Moses' likely refers to R. Moses ha-Kohen or R. Moses ibn Tibbon; resolved by inference only."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:39:30.515086277Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}